  "name": "Shift Type-working_hours_calculation_based_on-description",
  "property": "description",
  "property_type": "Text",
  "row_name": null,
  "value": "How a day's worked time is calculated for this shift — used both by Frappe's auto-attendance and by the Attendance Monitor timeline. <b>First Check-in and Last Check-out</b>: the whole span from the first to the last punch counts as worked, no breaks deducted (any punches in between are shown but don't split the time) — use for crews that don't track breaks (e.g. Vincitool). <b>Every Valid Check-in and Check-out</b>: punches are paired in/out, and only the paired intervals count — the gaps between pairs are treated as breaks and excluded."
